---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StaticPage from '../components/StaticPage.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — DivyaKatha"
  description="DivyaKatha is a quiet blog of temple tales and Hindu folklore from across India."
>
  <StaticPage
    title="About DivyaKatha"
    description="Temple tales, told gently."
  >
    <p>
      <strong>DivyaKatha</strong> (दिव्य कथा — "divine stories") is a small, story-first blog about the
      temples of India: the folklore woven into stone, the legends passed between generations, and the
      quiet reasons people still return to sacred places.
    </p>

    <p>
      Posts explore history, myth, and lived devotion — always as thoughtful storytelling, not as
      official religious doctrine or travel advice. If a tale varies by region or tradition, we try to
      say so.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs this site?</h2>
    <p>
      DivyaKatha is written and maintained by <strong>Rishabh Anand</strong>. Stories are researched
      and composed with care; corrections and suggestions are welcome.
    </p>

    <h2>How content is published</h2>
    <p>
      Articles are managed through a Strapi CMS and published on this Astro site. Images and text may
      be loaded from our content backend when you read a post.
    </p>

    <p>
      Have a question, correction, or story tip?
      <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </StaticPage>
</Base>
